const extraStepsEn = <String, List<String>>{
  'Sheera': ['Warm the milk with a little water and keep it hot nearby.', 'Roast rava in ghee on low heat for 4–5 minutes until fragrant and lightly golden.', 'Pour in the hot milk carefully (it will splutter) and stir to avoid lumps.', 'Add sugar and cardamom; cook covered for 2–3 minutes until soft and the ghee separates.', 'Top with chopped dry fruits and serve hot.'],
  'Kothimbir vadi': ['Chop a large bunch of coriander finely and mix with besan, rice flour, sesame seeds, chopped chilli and salt.', 'Add water little by little to make a thick, firm batter.', 'Shape into a log, steam for 15–20 minutes until a skewer comes out clean, and cool.', 'Cut into pieces and shallow-fry with a little oil until crisp and golden.', 'Serve hot with chutney or tea.'],
  'Sabudana vada': ['Soak sabudana for 4–6 hours until each pearl is soft, then drain very well.', 'Boil and mash the potato; mix with sabudana, crushed roasted peanuts, chopped chilli, cumin and salt.', 'Shape into flat round vadas with oiled hands.', 'Deep-fry on medium heat until golden and crisp, turning once.', 'Drain on paper and serve hot with curd or chutney.'],
  'Aloo paratha and curd': ['Knead a soft dough with wheat flour, salt and water; rest for 15 minutes.', 'Boil and mash potatoes; mix with chopped chilli, coriander and salt.', 'Stuff a ball of filling inside a ball of dough, seal well and roll gently.', 'Cook on a hot tawa with ghee until golden spots appear on both sides.', 'Serve hot with fresh curd.'],
  'Rava idli and chutney': ['Dry-roast rava for 3–4 minutes, cool, then mix with whisked curd, salt and water to a thick batter; rest for 20 minutes.', 'Temper mustard seeds, curry leaves and chopped chilli in a little oil and stir into the batter.', 'Grease idli moulds and fill them; steam for 10–12 minutes until a skewer comes out clean.', 'Grind coconut, chilli and a little curd or water with salt into a smooth chutney.', 'Serve the idlis hot with the chutney.'],
  'Zunka-bhakri': ['Heat oil; add mustard seeds, cumin, garlic and green chilli.', 'Add sliced onion and sauté until soft and light golden.', 'Lower the heat and sprinkle in besan slowly while stirring to avoid lumps; add salt and a splash of water.', 'Cover and cook for 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until dry and crumbly.', 'Serve hot with jowar bhakri.'],
  'Dal tadka and jeera rice': ['Rinse toor dal and pressure-cook with turmeric and salt until very soft; mash lightly.', 'Cook rice with a spoon of ghee and cumin until fluffy.', 'Heat ghee; add cumin, sliced garlic and chopped tomato and cook until soft.', 'Pour this tadka over the dal and simmer for 3–4 minutes.', 'Serve the dal with the jeera rice.'],
  'Bhendi masala and chapati': ['Wash okra, dry it completely and cut into rounds to avoid stickiness.', 'Fry okra in a little oil on medium heat until no longer sticky; set aside.', 'Sauté onion and tomato with spices into a thick masala.', 'Add the okra and salt, mix gently and cook covered for 5 minutes.', 'Serve hot with fresh chapati.'],
  'Paneer bhurji and chapati': ['Crumble the paneer coarsely with your hands.', 'Sauté chopped onion and green chilli in oil until soft; add tomato and spices and cook until the oil separates.', 'Add the paneer and salt and toss gently for 3–4 minutes; do not overcook.', 'Finish with chopped coriander.', 'Serve hot with chapati.'],
  'Shev bhaji and bhakri': ['Heat oil; add mustard seeds, then chopped onion and cook until golden.', 'Add tomato, goda masala and salt and cook into a thick, spicy gravy; add water for a curry-like consistency.', 'Add a little grated coconut and simmer for 5 minutes.', 'Stir in thick sev just before serving so it stays slightly firm.', 'Serve hot with bhakri.'],
  'Pav bhaji': ['Boil potato, cauliflower and peas until very soft and mash roughly.', 'Heat butter, add chopped tomato and spices and cook into a thick paste.', 'Add the mashed vegetables with a little water and cook for 10 minutes, mashing as it simmers.', 'Finish with a little more butter.', 'Toast pav in butter and serve with the hot bhaji.'],
  'Mushroom masala and chapati': ['Wipe mushrooms clean with a damp cloth (do not soak) and slice.', 'Sauté onion in oil until golden; add tomato and spices and cook into a thick masala.', 'Add mushrooms and salt; cook on high heat for 6–8 minutes until the water dries.', 'Simmer 2 minutes more and adjust salt.', 'Serve hot with chapati.'],
  'Aloo gobi and chapati': ['Cut potato and cauliflower into medium pieces and wash well.', 'Heat oil; add cumin, then tomato, turmeric and salt and cook until soft.', 'Add potato first with a splash of water and cook covered for 5 minutes.', 'Add cauliflower and cook covered until both are tender, stirring gently.', 'Serve hot with chapati.'],
  'Tomato saar and rice': ['Boil tomatoes with a little water, then blend into a smooth purée.', 'Heat ghee; add cumin and curry leaves, then pour in the purée.', 'Add grated coconut, salt and a little jaggery or sugar if the tomatoes are sour.', 'Simmer for 8–10 minutes and thin with water to a soupy consistency.', 'Serve hot over steamed rice.'],
  'Matar paneer and chapati': ['Cut paneer into cubes and soak in warm water for 10 minutes to keep it soft.', 'Sauté onion in oil until golden; add tomato and spices and cook until the oil separates; blend for a smooth gravy if you like.', 'Add peas and a cup of water; simmer for 8 minutes until the peas are tender.', 'Add the drained paneer and salt; simmer 3 minutes.', 'Serve hot with chapati.'],
  'Dal palak and rice': ['Pressure-cook toor dal with turmeric until soft; mash lightly.', 'Wash and chop the spinach.', 'Heat ghee; add cumin and sliced garlic, then the spinach and cook for 2–3 minutes.', 'Add the dal, salt and water as needed and simmer for 5 minutes.', 'Serve with hot steamed rice.'],
  'Batata vada': ['Boil and mash potatoes; temper mustard seeds, garlic and chopped chilli in a little oil and mix in with salt.', 'Shape into lemon-sized balls.', 'Make a thick batter of besan, salt and water.', 'Dip each ball in the batter and deep-fry on medium heat until golden.', 'Drain and serve hot with chutney.'],
  'Samosa': ['Knead a stiff dough with wheat flour, oil, salt and water; rest for 20 minutes.', 'Boil and mash potatoes; sauté with peas, cumin, chopped chilli and salt for the filling and cool.', 'Roll the dough thin, cut in half, shape each into a cone, fill and seal the edges with water.', 'Deep-fry on low to medium heat for 10–12 minutes until crisp and golden.', 'Drain and serve hot with chutney.'],
  'Corn chaat': ['Boil sweet corn kernels with a pinch of salt until tender and drain.', 'Toss the warm corn with a little butter.', 'Add chopped onion, tomato and coriander.', 'Season with lemon juice and salt.', 'Serve immediately.'],
  'Mutton curry and bhakri': ['Wash the mutton and marinate with ginger-garlic, salt and turmeric; keep refrigerated for at least 1 hour.', 'Brown sliced onion in oil; add goda masala and chopped tomato and cook until the oil separates.', 'Add the mutton and sear for 5–8 minutes.', 'Add hot water, cover and pressure-cook or simmer for 40–60 minutes until the meat is fully tender and cooked through.', 'Add grated coconut paste if you like, simmer 5 minutes and serve with bhakri.'],
  'Kolhapuri mutton and rice': ['Marinate mutton with ginger-garlic and salt in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour.', 'Dry-roast dry red chillies, coconut and spices and grind with onion into a fiery Kolhapuri masala.', 'Fry sliced onion until dark golden, add the masala and cook in oil until it darkens and the oil floats.', 'Add the mutton and hot water and pressure-cook or simmer for 40–60 minutes until very tender and cooked through.', 'Serve hot with rice (reduce the chillies for children).'],
  'Mutton biryani and raita': ['Marinate mutton with yogurt, ginger-garlic, salt and spices; keep refrigerated for at least 2 hours.', 'Brown sliced onion in ghee until deep golden; keep half aside.', 'Cook the marinated mutton with the onion and a little water until about three-quarters tender.', 'Parboil basmati rice with whole spices until 70% cooked; layer it over the mutton with the reserved onion.', 'Cover tightly and cook on low heat for 25–30 minutes; make sure the mutton is fully tender, then serve with raita.'],
  'Chicken sukka and chapati': ['Marinate chicken with ginger-garlic, salt and turmeric; keep refrigerated for 30 minutes.', 'Dry-roast coconut with spices until dark and grind coarsely.', 'Sauté onion in oil until golden, add the chicken and cook for 10 minutes, stirring.', 'Add the masala and a splash of water; cook covered until the chicken is fully cooked and the gravy is dry.', 'Serve hot with chapati.'],
  'Mutton kheema and pav': ['Wash the minced mutton and keep refrigerated until cooking.', 'Sauté onion in oil until golden; add ginger-garlic, tomato and spices and cook until the oil separates.', 'Add the mince and cook on high heat for 5 minutes, breaking up lumps.', 'Add peas and a little water, cover and cook for 25–30 minutes until the mince is fully cooked and dry.', 'Toast pav on a tawa and serve with the hot kheema.'],
  'Mutton pulao and raita': ['Marinate mutton with yogurt, ginger-garlic and salt; keep refrigerated for at least 1 hour.', 'Sauté whole spices and sliced onion until golden; add the mutton and cook for 10 minutes.', 'Add hot water and pressure-cook or simmer for 30–40 minutes until the mutton is nearly tender.', 'Add washed rice and the right amount of water (about 1.5 times the rice) and cook covered until the rice is done and the mutton is fully tender.', 'Rest 5 minutes and serve with raita.'],
  'Egg bhurji and chapati': ['Beat the eggs with a pinch of salt.', 'Sauté chopped onion, green chilli and tomato in oil until soft.', 'Pour in the eggs and stir gently on medium heat.', 'Cook until fully set and no liquid remains, then add coriander.', 'Serve hot with chapati.'],
  'Prawn curry and rice': ['Clean and devein the prawns; marinate with salt and turmeric and keep refrigerated.', 'Grind coconut with a small piece of tamarind and spices into a paste.', 'Sauté onion until golden, add the paste and cook for 5 minutes.', 'Add water and bring to a boil; add the prawns and cook for just 4–5 minutes until pink and opaque.', 'Serve hot with rice.'],
  'Kashmiri rogan josh and rice': ['Marinate mutton with yogurt, Kashmiri chilli powder, ginger-garlic and salt; keep refrigerated for at least 2 hours.', 'Heat ghee or oil; add whole spices, then the sliced onion and cook until deep golden.', 'Add the marinated mutton and cook on high heat for 8–10 minutes, stirring, until it browns and the oil separates.', 'Add hot water, cover and simmer or pressure-cook for 45–60 minutes until the meat is fully tender and cooked through.', 'Simmer uncovered for 5 minutes for a thick red gravy and serve with rice.'],
  'Saoji mutton and chapati': ['Marinate mutton with ginger-garlic and salt; keep refrigerated for at least 1 hour.', 'Dry-roast dry red chillies, coconut, poppy seeds, sesame seeds and whole spices separately until dark and fragrant, then grind with fried onion into a thick Saoji masala.', 'Heat oil and fry the masala well until the oil floats and the colour deepens.', 'Add the mutton and hot water; pressure-cook or simmer for 45–60 minutes until fully tender and cooked through.', 'Serve hot with chapati (very spicy: reduce the chillies for children).'],
  'Mutton sukka and bhakri': ['Marinate mutton with ginger-garlic, salt and turmeric; keep refrigerated for at least 1 hour.', 'Pressure-cook or simmer the mutton with a little water for 30–40 minutes until nearly tender.', 'Dry-roast dry red chillies, coconut and spices and grind coarsely.', 'Sauté onion in oil until golden, add the ground masala and cook until fragrant.', 'Add the mutton with its stock and cook uncovered until the gravy is dry and the meat is fully tender; serve with bhakri.'],
  'Mutton chops masala and chapati': ['Wash the mutton chops and marinate with yogurt, ginger-garlic, spices and salt; keep refrigerated for at least 2 hours.', 'Pressure-cook the chops with a little water for 20–25 minutes until tender; keep the stock.', 'Sauté onion and tomato in oil into a thick masala.', 'Add the chops and a little stock and cook for 10 minutes until the masala coats them.', 'Pan-fry on high heat for a few minutes for a browned finish and serve hot with chapati.'],
  'Mutton handi and chapati': ['Marinate mutton with yogurt, ginger-garlic and salt; keep refrigerated for at least 2 hours.', 'Heat ghee in a heavy pot (handi); add whole spices and sliced onion and cook until golden.', 'Add the mutton and tomato and cook on high heat for 8–10 minutes until the oil separates.', 'Add hot water, cover tightly and cook on low heat for 50–60 minutes until the meat is fully tender.', 'Serve hot from the pot with chapati.'],
  'Kheema pulao and raita': ['Wash minced mutton and marinate with yogurt, ginger-garlic and salt; keep refrigerated for 30 minutes.', 'Sauté whole spices and sliced onion in oil until golden.', 'Add the mince and cook on high heat for 8 minutes, breaking up lumps; add peas.', 'Add washed rice and water (about 1.5 times the rice), cover and cook on low heat until the rice and mince are fully cooked.', 'Rest 5 minutes, fluff and serve with raita.'],
};

